      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A workaround: If a private avatar which may contain some of this (permissible) inflammatory content (in private spaces) is uploaded for one-time use in private spaces and is deleted immediately after consenting parties have downloaded the avatar to see (or filtered by content gating), there's little or no risk of that avatar content ending up to be used in public spaces - an error robot will be shown to others, or you'll be forced back to the default VRChat robot avatar on the next app restart.\n\nWhile the avatar is deleted, it's also not directly reportable in-app because the content is already deleted (an error will be shown to the reporter), even if some parties see a cached version of it.",
